    "basis_definition": {
      "conversion": "8 pairs are market-ambiguous and split into 2 keys each: 76 + 8 = 84. R0's market_ambiguous=8 is the PAIR-basis count of the same population; on the key basis it is 16.",
      "key_basis": "KEY = (expert, instrument, market) — 84 keys",
      "pair_basis": "PAIR = (expert, instrument) — 76 pairs",
      "source": "R0 E_classify counted mutually exclusive buckets on the 76 (expert,instrument) PAIR basis and reported market_ambiguous=8. Each such pair is split into one key per market, so 8 pairs -> 16 keys, and 76 pairs + 8 extra market rows = 84 keys. The R0 number is neither a query bug nor a different population: it is the same population on the pair basis."
    },
